Updates in this release

New Features
* Added setting -transcript to the save command. It saves a transcript of the current session into a file
  in the output directory. Note that the filename is timestamped. In the transcript, commands are
  marked with ==>. The first line of the file is !TRANSCRIPT.
  * This makes it relatively easy to examine the transcript.
  * It also makes it possbile to consult the transscript to replay the commands. Note that during replay,
    the save -transcript command will be supressed. Also note that some commands will fail during replay
    simply becasue the DB is no longer in the same state as when the commands were originally issued.
    Some commands will be supressed (curently save -transcript, add, edit, bye, quit, exit and abort) during transcript consult.
    It is probably prudent to backup the DB before experimenting with such a transcript (remember, automatic
    backups are not yet implemented ... perhaps consult will at some point receive a -backup setting
    to backup the DB prior to execution of consult).

Bug fixes
* type/print of Programs was printing the ludes twice.
* Minor discrepancies around how the Lab version was shown. Note that in a release
  the version will always be of the form M.mR.0 (M=Major, m=minor). The last component
  (the 0) only changes in internal (non-released) builds.